  "output": {
    "answer": "That's not fully in the record. What I know is I flagged a one-in-three miss rate during the live demo of the scout, but I never stated a target number for the identification vote overall, or said whether two-in-three is good enough to ship. Other parts of the project do have explicit bars — one signal shape needs recall of at least 0.90, another needs a 90% precision floor — but those are pre-registered bars for specific pricing signals, not for the card-identification vote itself. So I can't tell you what number I'm targeting for the scout's overall accuracy, or whether two-in-three clears it.",
